    "q-61146": {
      "dom_id": "step-q61146",
      "name": "Question 3",
      "problem": "There are $35$ children in the fifth-grade class. If $40%$ of them have black hair, how many children have black hair?",
      "worked_solution": "To solve this problem, we can use the formula:\n\n$$\n\\text{part}=\\text{percentage}\\times \\text{whole}\n$$\n\nIn our case, the whole is the total number of children in the fifth-grade class, which is $35$ children. The percentage is $40%,$ and the part is the number of children with black hair.\n\n**Method 1**\n\nFirst, we convert the percentage to a decimal:\n\n$$\n40%=40÷100=0.4\n$$\n\nApplying our formula, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{part} & =\\text{percentage}\\times \\text{whole} \\\\  & =40%\\times 35 \\\\  & =0.4\\times 35 \\\\  & =14\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $40%$ of $35$ is $14.$ So, $14$ children have black hair.\n\n**Method 2**\n\nFirst, we convert the percentage to a fraction:\n\n$$\n40%=\\frac{40}{100}=\\frac{40÷20}{100÷20}=\\frac{2}{5}\n$$\n\nApplying our formula, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{part} & =\\text{percentage}\\times \\text{whole} \\\\  & =40%\\times 35 \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{5}\\times 35 \\\\  & =2\\times \\frac{35}{5} \\\\  & =2\\times 7 \\\\  & =14\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $40%$ of $35$ is $14.$ So, $14$ children have black hair.",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
