    "q-61163": {
      "dom_id": "step-q61163",
      "name": "Question 4",
      "problem": "A bunch of grapes contained $50$ grapes. Serena eats $28%$ of them. How many grapes did Serena eat?",
      "worked_solution": "To solve this problem, we can use the formula:\n\n$$\n\\text{part}=\\text{percentage}\\times \\text{whole}\n$$\n\nIn our case, the whole is the total number of grapes, which is $50$ grapes. The percentage is $28%,$ and the part is the number of grapes Serena ate.\n\n**Method 1**\n\nFirst, we convert the percentage to a decimal:\n\n$$\n28%=28÷100=0.28\n$$\n\nApplying our formula, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{part} & =\\text{percentage}\\times \\text{whole} \\\\  & =28%\\times 50 \\\\  & =0.28\\times 50 \\\\  & =14\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $28%$ of $50$ is $14.$ Thus, Serena ate $14$ grapes.\n\n**Method 2**\n\nFirst, we convert the percentage to a fraction:\n\n$$\n28%=\\frac{28}{100}=\\frac{28÷4}{100÷4}=\\frac{7}{25}\n$$\n\nApplying our formula, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{part} & =\\text{percentage}\\times \\text{whole} \\\\  & =28%\\times 50 \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{25}\\times 50 \\\\  & =7\\times \\frac{50}{25} \\\\  & =7\\times 2 \\\\  & =14\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $28%$ of $50$ is $14.$ Thus, Serena ate $14$ grapes.",
