      "name": "Question 5",
      "problem": "The original price of a toy robot in a department store was $$75.$ The store manager decides to reduce the price by $12%.$ How much of a discount has the manager given?",
      "worked_solution": "To find the discount, we can use the formula:\n\n$$\n\\text{part}=\\text{percentage}\\times \\text{whole}\n$$\n\nIn our case, the whole is the old price, which is $$75.$ The percentage is $12%,$ and the part is the discount in dollars.\n\n**Method 1**\n\nFirst, we convert the percentage to a decimal:\n\n$$\n12%=12÷100=0.12\n$$\n\nApplying our formula, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{part} & =\\text{percentage}\\times \\text{whole} \\\\  & =12%\\times 75 \\\\  & =0.12\\times 75 \\\\  & =9\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $12%$ of $75$ is $9.$ So, the discount is $$9.$\n\n**Method 2**\n\nFirst, we convert the percentage to a fraction:\n\n$$\n12%=\\frac{12}{100}=\\frac{12÷4}{100÷4}=\\frac{3}{25}\n$$\n\nApplying our formula, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{part} & =\\text{percentage}\\times \\text{whole} \\\\  & =12%\\times 75 \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{25}\\times 75 \\\\  & =3\\times \\frac{75}{25} \\\\  & =3\\times 3 \\\\  & =9\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $12%$ of $75$ is $9.$ So, the discount is $$9.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
