    "q-93049": {
      "dom_id": "step-q93049",
      "name": "Question 7",
      "problem": "Emma earns $$19,500$ a year. Of this amount, she must pay $12.6%$ in taxes. How much money should Emma pay in taxes?",
      "worked_solution": "To solve this problem, we can use the formula:\n\n$$\n\\text{part}=\\text{percentage}\\times \\text{whole}\n$$\n\nIn our case, the whole is the amount of money Emma earns annually, which is $$19,500.$ The percentage is $12.6%,$ and the part is the amount she must pay in taxes.\n\n**Method 1**\n\nFirst, we convert the percentage to a decimal:\n\n$$\n12.6%=12.6÷100=0.126\n$$\n\nApplying our formula, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{part} & =\\text{percentage}\\times \\text{whole} \\\\  & =12.6%\\times 19,500 \\\\  & =0.126\\times 19,500 \\\\  & =2,457\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $12.6%$ of $19,500$ is $2,457.$ Hence, Emma must pay $$2,457$ in taxes.\n\n**Method 2**\n\nFirst, we convert the percentage to a fraction:\n\n$$\n12.6%=\\frac{12.6}{100}\n$$\n\nApplying our formula, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{part} & =\\text{percentage}\\times \\text{whole} \\\\  & =12.6%\\times 19,500 \\\\  & =\\frac{12.6}{100}\\times 19,500 \\\\  & =12.6\\times \\frac{19,500}{100} \\\\  & =12.6\\times 195 \\\\  & =2,457\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $12.6%$ of $19,500$ is $2,457.$ Hence, Emma must pay $$2,457$ in taxes.",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
