    "q-61177": {
      "dom_id": "step-q61177",
      "name": "Question 9",
      "problem": "Margaret has $$1,500$ saved. Of this amount, she decides to spend $22.4%$ to buy some supplies for her farm. How much money does Margret plan to spend?",
      "worked_solution": "To solve this problem, we can use the formula:\n\n$$\n\\text{part}=\\text{percentage}\\times \\text{whole}\n$$\n\nIn our case, the whole is the amount of money Margaret has saved, which is $$1,500.$ The percentage is $22.4%,$ and the part is the amount of money that she decides to spend.\n\n**Method 1**\n\nFirst, we convert the percentage to a decimal:\n\n$$\n22.4%=22.4÷100=0.224\n$$\n\nApplying our formula, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{part} & =\\text{percentage}\\times \\text{whole} \\\\  & =22.4%\\times 1,500 \\\\  & =0.224\\times 1,500 \\\\  & =336\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $22.4%$ of $1,500$ is $336.$ Thus, Margaret plans to spend $$336.$\n\n**Method 2**\n\nFirst, we convert the percentage to a fraction:\n\n$$\n22.4%=\\frac{22.4}{100}\n$$\n\nApplying our formula, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{part} & =\\text{percentage}\\times \\text{whole} \\\\  & =22.4%\\times 1,500 \\\\  & =\\frac{22.4}{100}\\times 1,500 \\\\  & =22.4\\times \\frac{1,500}{100} \\\\  & =22.4\\times 15 \\\\  & =336\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $22.4%$ of $1,500$ is $336.$ Thus, Margaret plans to spend $$336.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
