    "q-61189": {
      "dom_id": "step-q61189",
      "name": "Question 12",
      "problem": "In his first season in the youth soccer league, Fernando scored $8$ goals. In his second season, he scored $250%$ of the number of goals he made in the first season. How many goals did Fernando score in his second season?",
      "worked_solution": "To solve this problem, we can use the formula:\n\n$$\n\\text{part}=\\text{percentage}\\times \\text{whole}\n$$\n\nIn our case, the whole is the number of goals Fernando scored in the first season, which is $8$ goals. The percentage is $250%,$ and the part is the number of goals Fernando scored in the second season.\n\n**Method 1**\n\nFirst, we convert the percentage to a decimal:\n\n$$\n250%=250÷100=2.5\n$$\n\nApplying our formula, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{part} & =\\text{percentage}\\times \\text{whole} \\\\  & =250%\\times 8 \\\\  & =2.5\\times 8 \\\\  & =20\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $250%$ of $8$ is $20.$ So, Fernando scored $20$ goals in his second season.\n\n**Method 2**\n\nFirst, we convert the percentage to a fraction:\n\n$$\n250%=\\frac{250}{100}=\\frac{250÷50}{100÷50}=\\frac{5}{2}\n$$\n\nApplying our formula, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{part} & =\\text{percentage}\\times \\text{whole} \\\\  & =250%\\times 8 \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{2}\\times 8 \\\\  & =\\frac{40}{2} \\\\  & =20\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $250%$ of $8$ is $20.$ So, Fernando scored $20$ goals in his second season.",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
