    "q-169407": {
      "dom_id": "step-q169407",
      "name": "Question 13",
      "problem": "In January $2022,$ a social media account had approximately $53,000$ followers. In December of that year, the account had $120%$ the number of followers it had in January. Determine the number of followers the account had in December, $2022.$",
      "worked_solution": "To solve this problem, we can use the formula:\n\n$$\n\\text{part}=\\text{percentage}\\times \\text{whole}\n$$\n\nIn our case, the whole is the number of followers the account had in January, $2022,$ which is $53,000.$ The percentage is $120%,$ and the part is the number of followers the account had in December $2022.$\n\n**Method 1**\n\nFirst, we convert the percentage to a decimal:\n\n$$\n120%=120÷100=1.2\n$$\n\nApplying our formula, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{part} & =\\text{percentage}\\times \\text{whole} \\\\  & =120%\\times 53,000 \\\\  & =1.2\\times 53,000 \\\\  & =63,600\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $120%$ of $53,000$ is $63,600.$ So, the social media account had $63,600$ followers in December $2022.$\n\n**Method 2**\n\nFirst, we convert the percentage to a fraction:\n\n$$\n120%=\\frac{120}{100}=\\frac{120÷20}{100÷20}=\\frac{6}{5}\n$$\n\nApplying our formula, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{part} & =\\text{percentage}\\times \\text{whole} \\\\  & =120%\\times 53,000 \\\\  & =\\frac{6}{5}\\times 53,000 \\\\  & =6\\times \\frac{53,000}{5} \\\\  & =6\\times 10,600 \\\\  & =63,600\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $120%$ of $53,000$ is $63,600.$ So, the social media account had $63,600$ followers in December $2022.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
