    "q-61184": {
      "dom_id": "step-q61184",
      "name": "Question 15",
      "problem": "In $2018$, Elena earned a salary of $$12,000.$ The following year, she earned $110%$ of the salary received in $2018.$ What was Elena's salary in $2019?$",
      "worked_solution": "To solve this problem, we can use the formula:\n\n$$\n\\text{part}=\\text{percentage}\\times \\text{whole}\n$$\n\nIn our case, the whole is the amount of money Elena earned in $2018$, which is $$12,000.$ The percentage is $110%,$ and the part is the amount of money she earned in $2019.$\n\n**Method 1**\n\nFirst, we convert the percentage to a decimal:\n\n$$\n110%=110÷100=1.1\n$$\n\nApplying our formula, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{part} & =\\text{percentage}\\times \\text{whole} \\\\  & =110%\\times 12,000 \\\\  & =1.1\\times 12,000 \\\\  & =13,200\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $110%$ of $12,000$ is $13,200.$ So, Elena earned $$13,200$ in $2019.$\n\n**Method 2**\n\nFirst, we convert the percentage to a fraction:\n\n$$\n110%=\\frac{110}{100}\n$$\n\nApplying our formula, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{part} & =\\text{percentage}\\times \\text{whole} \\\\  & =110%\\times 12,000 \\\\  & =\\frac{110}{100}\\times 12,000 \\\\  & =110\\times \\frac{12,000}{100} \\\\  & =110\\times 120 \\\\  & =13,200\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $110%$ of $12,000$ is $13,200.$ So, Elena earned $$13,200$ in $2019.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
            {
              "option": "a",
              "dom_id": "questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-61184-a",
